<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00878</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a792ff20-5857-4695-84f3-1fe9e5bcaec8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Function \(f\) gives the temperature, in degrees Celsius, \(t\) hours after midnight.</item>
</list>

<para>Choose which equation or expression represents the statement in function notation.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>The temperature was the same at 9 a.m. and at 4 p.m.</item>
  </list>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(f(9)=f(4)\)</item>
  <item>\(f(9)=f(16)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(f(9)=f(16)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>It was warmer at 9 a.m. than at 6 a.m.</item>
  </list>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(f(9)\)&gt;\(f(6)\)</item>
  <item>\(f(9)\)&lt;\(f(6)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(9)&gt;f(6)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>Some time after midnight, the temperature was 24 degrees Celsius.
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(f(24)=t\)</item>
  <item>\(f(0)&lt;24\)</item>
  <item>\(f(t)=24\)</item>
  <item>\(f(12)=24\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(t)=24\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Select the two points that are on the graph of \(f\) if we know that \(f(2)=-4\) and \(f(5)=3.4\).</item></list>
    <list>
      <item>\((-4, 2)\)</item>
      <item>\((2, -4)\)</item>
      <item>\((3.4, 5)\)</item>
      <item>\((5, 3.4)\)</item>
      <item>\((2, 5)\)</item>
    </list>
  
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((2, -4)\), \((5, 3.4)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Looking at the graph of the function, \(g\), below, which is greater, \(g(-5)\) or \(g(5)\)?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="A GRAPH OF FUNCTION G. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (−5, 2) AND (5, −3)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5a2c775e319efd946b6bd1f0ba070f76f6ce12ce"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item>\(g(-5)\) </item>
  <item>\(g(5)\) </item>
 </list> 
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> \(g(-5)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>The function \(T\) tells how many people are living on floor \(n\) of an apartment building. What does \(T(4)=82\) mean?</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>There are 82 people living on floor 4.</item>
  <item>There are 4 people living on floor 82.</item>
 </list> 
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>There are 82 people living on floor 4.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>The function \(T\) gives the temperature of a house, in degrees Fahrenheit, \(h\) hours after midnight. Choose which function notation represents the temperature at 6 a.m. was 70 degrees.</item></list>

    <list>
      <item>\(T(70)=6\)</item>
      <item>\(T(6)=70\)</item>
      <item>\(6(T)=70\)</item>
      <item>\(70(T)=6\)</item>
    </list>
  
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(T(6)=70\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>The graph below represents function \(f\), which gives the height of a drone, in meters, \(t\) seconds after it leaves the ground. Which statement describes the point \(f(2)=4\)?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, height, meters. Starting at 0 comma 0, the graph increases linearly. From 2 to 6, it’s horizontal. Then decreases linearly to 7 comma 0."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3192aada43883aac8e77e8ee8af08927d79ed818"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item>The height of the drone at 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.</item>
  <item>The height of the drone at 4 seconds is 2 meters off the ground</item>
</list>  
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.</para></section>
